data: {"type":"response.completed","sequence_number":2254,"safety_buffering":false,"response":{"id":"resp_07d23eca9328ceee016adf283475508191b59b0a9b663b7d9e","object":"response","created_at":1793009716,"completed_at":1793009747,"status":"completed","background":false,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"presence_penalty":0.0,"moderation":null,"model":"gpt-6.1-sol","access_programs":{"cyber":"standard"},"previous_response_id":null,"instructions":"You translate the supplied natural-language proof faithfully into Lean 4. Use the explicit project premises and any proved result in the pinned Mathlib environment. Preserve all assumptions, conclusions, equality modes and the supplied proof route. No reference answers, personal context, other tasks, shell or external services are available. Use the submit tool when the requested artifact is complete; if rejected, repair it. A strategy is advice, never an additional theorem or assumption. End this stage immediately when a submit tool reports stage_complete:true; the controller handles later stages. Within a proof stage, checked helper attempts are available through read_lean_draft. After a context reset, query its index before claiming no draft or helper exists. Helpers never become new premises. Use familiar interfaces directly; no background-note scan is required. For a relevant obstacle, select a matching local background_note_index entry and read_background_note if its details may help. Relate the actual Lean goal/context to its NL step: use the note grounds to identify a small missing application premise or transport, prove it from permitted inputs, then check the intended application. Verify actual types and conditions; a note is not a Lean proof or extra assumption. If it does not fit, continue ordinary allowed search or repair without insisting on that note or rebuilding a larger argument by default.","output":[{"type":"reasoning","id":"rs_07d23eca9328ceee016adf2836799c81918dc58c7632f26346","summary":[],"content":[],"encrypted_content":"gAAAAABq3yg2IqyySutaqiVmvIPv-It3i0UWRDKJv8J3KiRzUa6NzfN1MOtU1kDCcQ6Yc3EmcLSCgPnBuytUl50vD6iwZbyRkvFnhySzR8cT9LfBfVMnVHSbTgN2iBJJT1VKEomfjOtHop1q9KUKEOMbwSUpmwOqotSxt6P5O1-EgTXUr4gboOUHLl92ktPxevMRdKNyJgudApOF9imGuzzmJIfKN6yP8-hwZJ1BQOApf9o4Qj83R7nbzl-sx5hrD4BW8sgfjFQpF-mSW4MQ2ZEtIreFDABntRlI20H6y09QCl71TzfANl1XtGEvfRevykUtVc9eZGg_BWT0xP-sQ3N7jbR4qrUQbk8SKyIc3FJtVKSBEz51zf4dQw2btWORHUoKo1MzQaPEmE8AYk_IG_FrKOoNE5SA3k5DAgGeyf_uobIJzgSlq1Kfrnr5JBQ6NaXcfsUPecB-9b5-GzoOjaTmAQrrnn9TMqncIQuamER402D-YBqufnAzxRwCPNrpeUC64tihDxHSfOYkXjxCpH-N-5AEoEtN6fQM7pYnoR6ugCXrrxz4n5wnNmwhri2iH81LE9R2KLPVtM_Xcb5laNgIL5TJYsinHXku_nBSzBRuDQ8G9oL-AeeJEZgNTyA2msCSCRjYrNpNzoliIEIYCwK87lB-iXNSEk4l6KmpHsrayiEBBvlUNxcV2rSWMpxj_e_pMs-eKafA7-WSEklMO5WA59sfsXHRFuIrVlk_DOTGIRSJ0PVhYqujcuzGuTbyXwcy8yrrJvlt9xgEtLqO6XcmhV3OWt8PZIkdOuw1BY7MGV228jHmPRE6uyo5bH8HJ2ghnuXDDfD1WQSHHIdq3wKwgNgXy4GTavjfGQ24-zQETas_yZ5-F0qucBhoqBDTQ3zdwBi6KIcowRz7UhU578c-TO6H6XnBkumvjfDH8c7ZCLUJe3Y4nHBEp91UAHYzNWi5Z8e-PT011mRkZ5PoLZhgG8JsrjCjBqu6XYEHbPQs_Q5m0XWRyn6E5UuUlWuSrQo575UCNvDtQk_Uc7jnXk6SPjjZ9lSOEgo_h5nfmF6hn4kucf8do72aTg_nJxIdLRjzyjNSo2KDDA0rsoKYpIzeLZjbznQlApindyF-EyQbDzK2JkldLWq-LgnE2gHTBGJsZ9AZJJLBLzY3dktpmc7nwvMXEgf2AMFd48YAdTCfOb_legct08PZT_meIE_5Wjx24cPAFKcg1dg0iO5bhO1L6kpXNf3yRt1N9hJ267LUkU7gaGQWLMYbVVBFh2ooBkqoreO2R4TS-jrg3uPZigzlrv5f6WjhgG3fyZ2MYoLkpHPbevOmwDRrQmR8Ksi2qngctJ_Kteir81hR-1ylzZCkxRSMEIem0_MvJ90mJZt7OYHeLPdDmy3qD0_uCuSpqCjB1I9KPvwA7qMlPNe6pRJWTJ61xBfQHj1-GFp1l8StBljma90wa6OpYRXnAFdFr8B55HUj-WXSCYqVROVnb3LBH6vX6n-kBpLiaolOmSHPvstp_wz-4JnJ90ptQuJpsO_xIabyUhLaqmRWzs1oLFUTn4b5K2VdJKWuhXMT3GgAX0-BqR5G3eeUN22cqGvASRNcSaW-mLroBW0GeZ1-zy4M-zsh_JHnLSORDuV-ycmgYf4v3XpH1Jd_FqYi89gYKQb83flo57kc"},{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_07d23eca9328ceee016adf2836a5b48191ac940c29e6c062e6","call_id":"call_0171a18d20364ad2aa0229385591ddca","name":"check_transition","arguments":"{\"proof\":\"classical\\nhave dx_smooth : ∀ {V : Type} [NormedAddCommGroup V] [NormedSpace ℝ V] (f : WM.X n × ℝ → V), ContDiffOn ℝ ∞ f (WM.dom n) → ∀ j : Fin n, ContDiffOn ℝ ∞ (fun p : WM.X n × ℝ => WM.dx f j p.1 p.2) (WM.dom n) := by\\n  intro V _ _ f hf j\\n  have hopen : IsOpen (WM.dom n) := isOpen_lt continuous_const continuous_snd\\n  intro p hp\\n  have hfp : ContDiffAt ℝ ∞ (Function.uncurry (fun (p : WM.X n × ℝ) (y : WM.X n) => f (y,p.2))) (p,p.1) := (hf.contDiffAt (hopen.mem_nhds hp)).comp _ (contDiffAt_snd.prodMk (contDiffAt_fst.snd))\\n  have hd := ContDiffAt.fderiv (f := fun (p : WM.X n × ℝ) (y : WM.X n) => f (y,p.2)) (g := fun p => p.1) hfp contDiffAt_fst (m := (∞ : WithTop ℕ∞)) (by simp)\\n  exact (hd.clm_apply contDiffAt_const).contDiffWithinAt\\nhave const_derivs : ∀ {V : Type} [NormedAddCommGroup V] [NormedSpace ℝ V] (O : Set (WM.X n × ℝ)), IsOpen O → ∀ (f : WM.X n × ℝ → V) (v : V), Set.EqOn f (fun _ => v) O → ∀ p ∈ O, WM.dt f p.1 p.2 = 0 ∧ ∀ j, WM.dx f j p.1 p.2 = 0 := by\\n  intro V _ _ O hO f v hf p hp\\n  have he : f =ᶠ[𝓝 p] (fun _ => v) := Filter.eventually_of_mem (hO.mem_nhds hp) hf\\n  constructor\\n  · have ht : (fun r => f (p.1,r)) =ᶠ[𝓝 p.2] (fun _ => v) := he.comp_tendsto (continuous_const.prodMk continuous_id).continuousAt\\n    simpa [WM.dt] using ht.deriv_eq\\n  · intro j\\n    have hx : (fun y => f (y,p.2)) =ᶠ[𝓝 p.1] (fun _ => v) := he.comp_tendsto (continuous_id.prodMk continuous_const).continuousAt\\n    simp [WM.dx, hx.fderiv_eq]\\nhave make_good : ∀ (C : Set (WM.X n)) (R : ℝ), IsCompact C → IsCompact (WM.box n R) → ∀ f : WM.X n → ℝ, Continuous f → (∀ x, x ∉ C → f x = 0) → WM.good C R f := by\\n  intro C R hC hQ f hf hz\\n  have hs : HasCompactSupport f := HasCompactSupport.of_support_subset_isCompact hC (by\\n    intro x hx\\n    by_contra h\\n    exact hx (hz x h))\\n  obtain ⟨B,hB,hbound⟩ := (hQ.image hf).isBounded.exists_pos_norm_le\\n  refine ⟨hf, ⟨B, hB.le, ?_⟩, hz, hf.integrable_of_hasCompactSupport hs⟩\\n  intro x hx\\n  simpa only [Real.norm_eq_abs] using hbound (f x) (Set.mem_image_of_mem f hx)\\nrcases h_T002 with ⟨hut, hutt, hxu, he, het, hident, hmixed⟩\\nhave ha : ContDiffOn ℝ ∞ (WM.aTerm u) (WM.dom n) := hut.inner hutt\\nhave hb : ∀ j, ContDiffOn ℝ ∞ (WM.bTerm u j) (WM.dom n) := fun j => (hxu j).inner (dx_smooth _ hut j)\\nhave hc : ∀ j, ContDiffOn ℝ ∞ (WM.cTerm u j) (WM.dom n) := fun j => hut.inner (dx_smooth _ (hxu j) j)\\nhave hf : ∀ j, ContDiffOn ℝ ∞ (WM.flux u j) (WM.dom n) := fun j => hut.inner (hxu j)\\nhave hd : ∀ j, ContDiffOn ℝ ∞ (WM.divFlux u j) (WM.dom n) := fun j => dx_smooth _ (hf j) j\\nhave local_all : ∀ τ : ℝ, 0 < τ → ∃ C R, WM.localData u q τ C R := by\\n  intro τ hτ\\n  obtain ⟨C,R,hgeom⟩ := h_T003 τ hτ\\n  obtain ⟨hC,hR,hCQ,hconst⟩ := hgeom\\n  have hboxeq : WM.box n R = Set.Icc (fun _ : Fin n => -R) (fun _ : Fin n => R) := by\\n    ext x\\n    simp [WM.box, Set.mem_Icc, Pi.le_def, forall_and]\\n  have hQ : IsCompact (WM.box n R) := hboxeq ▸ isCompact_Icc\\n  have hv : volume (WM.box n R) = ENNReal.ofReal ((2*R)^n) := by\\n    rw [hboxeq, Real.volume_Icc_pi]\\n    simp [sub_neg_eq_add, ← two_mul, ENNReal.ofReal_pow, le_of_lt hR]\\n  let O : Set (WM.X n × ℝ) := Cᶜ ×ˢ Set.Ioo (τ/2) (3*τ/2)\\n  have hO : IsOpen O := hC.isClosed.isOpen_compl.prod isOpen_Ioo\\n  have huO : Set.EqOn u (fun _ => q) O := by\\n    intro p hp\\n    exact hconst p.1 hp.1 p.2 ⟨hp.2.1.le, hp.2.2.le⟩\\n  have hutO : Set.EqOn (WM.ut u) (fun _ => 0) O := by\\n    intro p hp\\n    exact (const_derivs O hO u q huO p hp).1\\n  have hxuO : ∀ j, Set.EqOn (WM.xu u j) (fun _ => 0) O := by\\n    intro j p hp\\n    exact (const_derivs O hO u q huO p hp).2 j\\n  have heO : Set.EqOn (WM.e u) (fun _ => 0) O := by\\n    intro p hp\\n    simp [WM.e, hutO hp, fun j => hxuO j hp]\\n  have hetO : Set.EqOn (WM.et u) (fun _ => 0) O := by\\n    intro p hp\\n    exact (const_derivs O hO (WM.e u) 0 heO p hp).1\\n  have haO : Set.EqOn (WM.aTerm u) (fun _ => 0) O := by\\n    intro p hp\\n    simp [WM.aTerm, hutO hp]\\n  have hbO : ∀ j, Set.EqOn (WM.bTerm u j) (fun _ => 0) O := by\\n    intro j p hp\\n    simp [WM.bTerm, hxuO j hp]\\n  have hcO : ∀ j, Set.EqOn (WM.cTerm u j) (fun _ => 0) O := by\\n    intro j p hp\\n    simp [WM.cTerm, hutO hp]\\n  have hfO : ∀ j, Set.EqOn (WM.flux u j) (fun _ => 0) O := by\\n    intro j p hp\\n    simp [WM.flux, hutO hp]\\n  have hdO : ∀ j, Set.EqOn (WM.divFlux u j) (fun _ => 0) O := by\\n    intro j p hp\\n    exact (const_derivs O hO (WM.flux u j) 0 (hfO j) p hp).2 j\\n  refine ⟨C,R, ⟨hC,hR,hCQ,hconst⟩, hQ, hv, hv ▸ ENNReal.ofReal_lt_top, ?_, ?_⟩\\n  · intro x hx r hr k hk\\n    have hp : (x,r) ∈ O := ⟨hx,hr⟩\\n    have heq : u =ᶠ[𝓝 (x,r)] (fun _ => q) := Filter.eventually_of_mem (hO.mem_nhds hp) huO\\n    rw [(heq.iteratedFDeriv ℝ k).eq_of_nhds, iteratedFDeriv_const_of_ne (ne_of_gt hk)]\\n  · intro r hr\\n    have hrpos : 0 < r := by linarith [hr.1]\\n    have section_good : ∀ (f : WM.X n × ℝ → ℝ), ContDiffOn ℝ ∞ f (WM.dom n) → Set.EqOn f (fun _ => 0) O → WM.good C R (fun x => f (x,r)) := by\\n      intro f hfs hz\\n      apply make_good C R hC hQ\\n      · exact hfs.continuousOn.comp_continuous (continuous_id.prodMk continuous_const) (fun x => hrpos)\\n      · intro x hx\\n        exact hz ⟨hx,hr⟩\\n    exact ⟨section_good _ he heO, section_good _ het hetO, section_good _ ha haO,\\n      fun j => ⟨section_good _ (hb j) (hbO j), section_good _ (hc j) (hcO j), section_good _ (hd j) (hdO j)⟩⟩\\nrefine ⟨⟨hut,hutt,hxu,he,het,hident,hmixed⟩, ?_, local_all⟩\\nintro t ht\\nobtain ⟨C,R,hlocal⟩ := local_all t ht\\nhave htI : t ∈ Set.Ioo (t/2) (3*t/2) := by constructor <;> linarith\\nexact (hlocal.2.2.2.2.2 t htI).1.2.2.2\"}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"Search the pinned mathlib Lean source using a regular expression; at most 100 lines.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"Read specified lines of a Mathlib/*.lean source file from the pinned checkout.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"line_count":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start_line","line_count"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_transition","description":"Compile a tactic body for the fixed target; no leading by, declarations, or placeholders.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"proof":{"type":"string"}},"required":["proof"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_transition","description":"Submit and check the final tactic body for the same target.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"proof":{"type":"string"}},"required":["proof"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_auxiliary","description":"Compile one helper proposition and tactic body in exactly this local port context. This never accepts the final goal or adds a premise.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"statement":{"type":"string"},"proof":{"type":"string"}},"required":["statement","proof"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_lean_draft","description":"Read only your own same-stage proof/helper attempts. kind=index lists attempts; proof/auxiliary returns the selected body lines and actual check. No other stage or file is accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"kind":{"type":"string","enum":["index","proof","auxiliary"]},"candidate":{"type":"integer"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["kind","candidate","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_background_note","description":"Read one complete audited background note from this task index by its qualified ID. No other task, file or proof is accessible; this is guidance, not a checked Lean proof.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false}],"tool_choice":"auto","parallel_tool_calls":false,"prompt_cache_key":"0a6d353c-a562-498d-a34a-b7f85027092b","prompt_cache_retention":"24h","text":{"format":{"type":"text"},"verbosity":"low"},"top_p":0.98,"top_logprobs":0,"temperature":1.0,"reasoning":{"effort":"high","context":"all_turns","summary":null,"mode":"standard"},"user":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":21294,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":18944,"cache_write_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2414,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":13},"total_tokens":23708,"attribution":{"items":{"fc_07d23eca9328ceee016adf27c7f65c819193243a88d0514d16":{"input_tokens":39,"cached_tokens":39,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_07d23eca9328ceee016adf27cf9ee48191b352923053c1fd1a":{"input_tokens":25,"cached_tokens":25,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_07d23eca9328ceee016adf27d261408191ad291f3f793f8b97":{"input_tokens":55,"cached_tokens":55,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_07d23eca9328ceee016adf27e1a97c8191924ae63cfc313b1e":{"input_tokens":269,"cached_tokens":269,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_07d23eca9328ceee016adf27f03fe081918ac5bb1f7aa081f2":{"input_tokens":44,"cached_tokens":44,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_07d23eca9328ceee016adf27f463c081919fb33a50d1be5114":{"input_tokens":316,"cached_tokens":316,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_07d23eca9328ceee016adf2800376c8191b9a809f7b3487044":{"input_tokens":309,"cached_tokens":309,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_07d23eca9328ceee016adf280a90f0819183c27788e99f5209":{"input_tokens":45,"cached_tokens":45,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_07d23eca9328ceee016adf280f13d08191b32c5e306e269a30":{"input_tokens":234,"cached_tokens":234,"cache_write_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"fc_